{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLNm1Egzkw2ia6Zjospe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the wrong `apart` result. `bug.apart(t)` now returns `-a*t + a/2 - a/(2*(2*t - 1))`, which matches the `a=1` case from the issue.\n\n**Cause:** in `apart` (`sympy/polys/partfrac.py`), the polynomial division ran over the ring `ZZ[a]`, where `div` quietly dropped the remainder. The fix converts `P` and `Q` to a field (`ZZ(a)`) just before the division. It's one added line.\n\n**Tests:** I ran `sympy/polys/tests/test_partfrac.py`. 10 pass and `test_noncommutative_pseudomultivariate` fails. That test fails the same way on the unmodified code, so my change didn't cause it. I didn't look into why it fails. I didn't add a regression test, since the rules say not to touch test files."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":995,"cache_read_input_tokens":26553,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":995},"output_tokens":290,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"48191fee-04c5-4aa3-971d-19b09231f24e","uuid":"8024e3f6-1cc4-4016-bbe7-579a5aa8e3ed","timestamp":"2026-11-23T19:01:00.679Z","request_id":"req_011ChLNkzr8d76Z3J4eAK1Wj"}
